<section vertical-align="center">
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item>
      <h2>Map equipment and substances before mapping sectors</h2>
      <p>For each holding, establish five coordinates before concluding on exposure.</p>
      <grid recipe="process-steps" spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug">
        <grid-item colspan="12">
          <h4>Substance</h4>
          <p>ODS, HFC, lower-impact substitute, or unknown.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="12">
          <h4>Asset</h4>
          <p>Refrigeration, HVAC, foam, fire suppression, or industrial process.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="12">
          <h4>Lifecycle</h4>
          <p>Installation, servicing, replacement, recovery, or disposal.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="12">
          <h4>Value channel</h4>
          <p>Capex, operating cost, downtime, compliance, or customer access.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="12">
          <h4>Action</h4>
          <p>Underwrite, reserve, engage, monitor, or defer.</p>
        </grid-item>
      </grid>
      <aside variant="note">
        <p><b>Investment implication:</b> a sector label cannot substitute for equipment and substance evidence.</p>
      </aside>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>